strate significant variability, particularly in the later months. I'll need to complete the data set to calculate the precise correlation between these variables.\n\nI notice the September data appears problematic, with conflicting values for grand total and American vessels across different table sections. This inconsistency requires careful verification to ensure accurate statistical analysis.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_d5590a29e74244b9bf9cb216","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# First table data - net registered tonnage (thousands of tons)\n# Looking at 1941 columns: Jan through Sept\ngrand_total_1941 = [1825, 1801, 2032, 2662, 3694, 4177, 4791, 4657, 3837]\namerican_1941 = [468, 489, 553, 680, 940, 1068, 1041, 930, 825]\n\n# Calculate percentage for Jan, Feb, Mar 1941\ngrand_total_jfm = [1825, 1801, 2032]\namerican_jfm = [468, 489, 553]\n\ntotal_american = sum(american_jfm)\ntotal_grand = sum(grand_total_jfm)\npercentage = (total_american / total_grand) * 100\n\nprint(f\"Total American (Jan-Mar): {total_american}\")\nprint(f\"Total Grand (Jan-Mar): {total_grand}\")\nprint(f\"Percentage: {percentage:.1f}%\")\n\n# Calculate Pearson correlation for the full 1941 series\nn = len(grand_total_1941)\nmean_x = sum(grand_total_1941) / n\nmean_y = sum(american_1941) / n\n\nprint(f\"\\nMean Grand Total: {mean_x}\")\nprint(f\"Mean American: {mean_y}\")\n\nnumerator = sum((grand_total_1941[i] - mean_x) * (american_1941[i] - mean_y) for i in range(n))\ndenominator_x = math.sqrt(sum((x - mean_x)**2 for x in grand_total_1941))\ndenominator_y = math.sqrt(sum((y - mean_y)**2 for y in american_1941))\n\ncorrelation = numerator / (denominator_x * denominator_y)\n\nprint(f\"\\nPearson correlation (full 1941 series): {correlation:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Correlation (3 decimal places): {round(correlation, 3)}\")\n\n# Also verify with 3 points only\nprint(\"\\n--- With 3 data points only (Jan-Mar) ---\")\nn3 = 3\nmean_x3 = sum(grand_total_jfm) / n3\nmean_y3 = sum(american_jfm) / n3\n\nnum3 = sum((grand_total_jfm[i] - mean_x3) * (american_jfm[i] - mean_y3) for i in range(n3))\nden_x3 = math.sqrt(sum((x - mean_x3)**2 for x in grand_total_jfm))\nden_y3 = math.sqrt(sum((y - mean_y3)**2 for y in american_jfm))\n\ncorr3 = num3 / (den_x3 * den_y3)\nprint(f\"Correlation (3 points): {corr3:.6f}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
